{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-217812","model_call":12,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"positive canthal tilt\" (+ natural born genetics inherited))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"positive canthal tilt\" (+ natural born genetics inherited))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_59_603346943#9_1468447829","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2536","rank":1,"snippet":"Preventing Premature Dropping of the Canthi Types of Canthal Tilt How to Determine Your Canthal Tilt How to Prevent Premature Dropping of the Canthi Canthal Tilt Correction: Canthopexy vs. Canthoplasty Canthal Tilt Surgery and Blepharoplasty \" , \"segment\": \"Usually, the procedure involves splitting the canthal angle and cutting the lateral canthal tendon away from the lateral orbital rim. The lower lid is then shortened and a new lateral canthal angle created using stitches. During outer canthoplasty, the lateral canthus is tightened and elevated. This allows the surgeon to accurately restore a <cover>positive canthal tilt, and ideally create a more natural </cover>appearance. Lateral canthoplasty can be used during any form of lower eyelid surgery. If the patient already has a positive canthal tilt, the surgeon may still perform canthoplasty for extra support so the positive tilt will endure. As Schlessinger notes, technically standard eyelid surgery (blepharoplasty) does not address canthal tilt nor change the shape of the eye. Instead, it is meant to improve the appearance of tired or baggy eyelids. However, as Truswell points out, canthal tilt is taken into account during the initial consultation for those considering blepharoplasty. Assessing canthal tilt is an important part ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_59_603346943#9_1468447829","rank":1,"relevance":1}]},"time":55},"model_calls":12,"document_judgments":7,"relevance_3":0,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"request","topic_id":"2024-217812","model_call":12,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2536"},"model_calls":12,"document_judgments":7,"relevance_3":0,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-217812","model_call":12,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2536"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q2536"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1370231623#7_2504756757","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2536","rank":2,"snippet":"Canthal Tilt Correction Canthoplasty Positive Canthal Tilt Neutral Canthal Tilt \" , \"segment\": \"A popular procedures is upper eyelid and lower eyelid blepharoplasty. During every preoperative cosmetic plastic surgery consultation, canthal tilt is carefully assessed. At Ocean Drive Plastic Surgery, we aim to correct canthal tilt to withn 5-9 degrees of positivity as this is a cornerstone of periorbital aesthetics. We augment every lower lid blepharoplasty with a procedure called a lateral retincular canthoplasty. This innovative procedure tightens and elevates the lateral canthus allowing us to accurately recreate the <cover>positive canthal tilt of your youth and providing for a natural </cover>look. Canthoplasty Our canthoplasty can be utilized on any type of lower eyelid procedure. We commonly complex it with lower eyelid spetal reset procedures in both men and women. As well it is always combined with transconjunctival lower eyelid approaches too. Recreation of positive canthal tilt is a required part of Dr. Durkin’s lower eyelid blepharoplasty procedures. In patients who have preexisting positive tilt, Dr. Durkin supports the existing tilt with a support canthoplasty.\" , \"start_char\": 2495.000000 , \"title\": \"Canthal Tilt | Cosmetic ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_59_603346943#9_1468447829","rank":1,"relevance":1}]},"time":11},"model_calls":12,"document_judgments":7,"relevance_3":0,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
