Academy of Facial Plastic & Reconstructive Surgery ( AAFPRS ). A neutral canthal tilt occurs when no angle exists between the medial canthus and lateral canthus. “ When the line is flat it is a neutral tilt.","ok":true,"op":"document"},"time":16},"model_calls":19,"document_judgments":14,"relevance_3":0,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
